    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "Solve the following. $4x^2-12x+5=0$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\dfrac12,\\dfrac52$.\n\nFactorise as $(2x-1)(2x-5)=0$ and use the null factor law.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4x^2-12x+5&=4x^2-10x-2x+5\\\\4x^2-12x+5&=2x(2x-5)-(2x-5)\\\\4x^2-12x+5&=(2x-1)(2x-5).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(2x-1)(2x-5)=0$. By the null factor law, $2x-1=0$ or $2x-5=0$.\n$$x=\\frac12\\text{ or }x=\\frac52.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
